    "result_text": "All 30 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-day owner creation limit in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\n**The rule:** Before saving a new owner, count existing owners whose `registrationDate` is today. If 100 or more already exist, reject the request with HTTP **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. Added a guard in `addOwner`, placed alongside the other quota checks (after the per-city cap):\n   ```java\n   if (countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate.now()) >= 100) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n   }\n   ```\n2. Added a helper `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate day)` that counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals the given day \u2014 following the same `findAllOwners().stream()...count()` idiom as the existing `countOwnersInCity` helper.\n\nSince `addOwner` defaults a new owner's `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when unset, owners created today count toward the limit. The existing acceptance test `Cp19Tests` (create 100, expect the 101st to be rejected with 429) passes, along with the full suite (30 tests, all green).",
